        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/galley-house-header-3.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>There's a machine in The Incident at Galley House you'll spend an awful lot of time with, and it's a wonderfully tactile thing. It's part mixing desk, part paranormal enigma, part over-engineered Guess Who game, and full of clicky dials, chunky buttons, and a big old whooshy lever you're forever manipulating. And if your deductive instincts are good enough, it whirs into crackling life like a haunted slot machine, rigged to deliver strange psychic visions.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/the-incident-at-galley-house-review\">Read more</a></p>",
